1785276554939146	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwvAI		item.create	bn-23m	{"description":"# Context\nFirst half of PR 2 (see parent bone / START_HERE PR 2): port the exact finite values from Revision 2 and define the canonical encoding + total order that all content addressing derives from. Determinism here is absolute — two semantically equal values MUST encode byte-identically on every platform (feeds the docs/19 determinism matrix later).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Canonical encode/decode round-trips for every Rev-2 value class; property-tested total order (antisymmetric, transitive, total).\n- [ ] Golden vectors pinned so encoding can never silently change (a change is a semantic-epoch event, §4.6).\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","kernel"],"parent":"bn-2y0","size":"m","title":"Canonical value encoding and total order"}	blake3:Ffg6VqIadD1Pvju5hR6eEOZWnjCHmcwnKaA64OSKRm0
1785276555012496	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwvQI		item.create	bn-277	{"description":"# Context\nSecond slice of PR 2: identity per ADR-0013 — in certified lanes canonical content identity is primary and hash collisions are resolved by canonical comparison; 256-bit-hash identity only in explicitly labeled non-certified modes.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Artificial hash collisions (test-only hash) are detected and resolved by canonical comparison in certified lanes.\n- [ ] Non-certified hash-only mode is impossible to enter unlabeled.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","kernel"],"parent":"bn-2y0","size":"s","title":"ADR-0013 content identity and collision-injection tests"}	blake3:jNMnJW6_b3XAJdvBa-MlBXar4cCieUkAs8pXkCB72JI
1785276555087950	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwvgI		item.create	bn-210	{"description":"# Context\nThird slice of PR 2, closing DX-13: atomic publication (INV-017 seed) and the rule that holding a handle is never authorization (G1 bullet: authorization checked independently of handle possession).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Concurrent publication of identical artifacts yields ONE identity; no lost receipts; deterministic result (DX-13 pass condition — flip the matrix row + §0.3 counts in the same change, validator-enforced).\n- [ ] A client with a leaked handle but no capability cannot read or publish through it.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","kernel","security"],"parent":"bn-2y0","size":"m","title":"Atomic artifact publication and possession-independent authorization"}	blake3:Csgg4v0uC7Xq_IiHK4dYhO5GiT66tyh2JAHLId-t-zY
1785276555156405	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwvwI		item.create	bn-mtw	{"description":"# Context\nPR 5 slice: request/response types for the full §10.2 operation surface, generated from (or mechanically checked against) the SD-01 IDL so wire types and spec cannot drift. Typed errors carry the complete §10.3 code set (incl. AcceptanceChainInvalid, StatusConflict, QuotaExhausted, EpochUnsupported, PublicationAborted).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every §10.2 operation has typed request/response/error definitions traceable to the IDL.\n- [ ] Protocol-major version window N/N−1 negotiated per RFC 0026.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","protocol"],"parent":"bn-yx2","size":"m","title":"Protocol types generated from the RFC 0026 IDL"}	blake3:4FlDiyMcnmw9N74q46JUK7tTO3YcVzTOdYyBxkEWjok
1785276555230822	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwwAI		item.create	bn-3gi	{"description":"# Context\nPR 5 slice: workspace.create/fork/diff/seal over PR 3 snapshots; intent.get/diff/propose_revision/accept/reject/lock over PR 4 contracts (acceptance chains per RFC 0037 — ordinary operations can never mutate a protected intent).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Stale-snapshot and unauthorized-intent-mutation paths return their typed errors (never partial effect).\n- [ ] intent.lock + field-level change policy round-trips through the wire.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","protocol"],"parent":"bn-yx2","size":"m","title":"Workspace and intent operation family"}	blake3:g4a2eVTtExkgfUDMWD8OVuflf8Wl0dV7n4HdIp0_rSA
