1785276555952316	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwygI		item.create	bn-2he	{"description":"# Context\nPR 9 slice: the covenant made mechanical — <15,000 non-test lines across the four crates enforced in CI (docs/03); mutation tests over certificate fields; receipt generation with checker epoch, build digest, input hashes.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CI fails if the four-crate non-test line count exceeds 15,000.\n- [ ] Every single-field certificate mutation in the suite is rejected (PR 9 exit).\n- [ ] Receipts carry checker epoch + build digest + input hashes (INV-014 seed).\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","kernel"],"parent":"bn-6tv","size":"m","title":"Kernel covenant enforcement: line budget, mutation suite, receipts"}	blake3:OAXnF1lI_ELgIDUq-q1Ig8znzxb0vuX4L1r57KRvoGI
1785276556021750	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwywI		item.create	bn-ymw	{"description":"# Context & Background\nA Phase A EXIT condition and standing G2 bullet with no owning PR in START_HERE: \"the prompt-injection corpus cannot trigger privileged operations\" (plan §21 Phase A exit, §22 G2, §18). Build the corpus (injection payloads embedded in workspace files, intent text, evidence content, Context Pack fields) and harden the privileged-operation paths (intent mutation, evidence promotion, policy overrides) against it. Related: research/35 workbench-security lane (red-team corpus grows from this seed).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Corpus of injection attempts across every agent-readable artifact class, run in CI.\n- [ ] Zero privileged operations triggered; injections surface as inert data, and capability checks (not output filtering) are the enforcement mechanism.\n# Serves\nWithout this, agent-facing artifacts are an attack channel into the very promotion machinery the plan exists to protect.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","security","aci"],"parent":"bn-19p","size":"m","title":"Prompt-injection corpus and privileged-operation hardening [G2]"}	blake3:tB9RNpq9un7pbQ_ObreFRtA_hLdx23v1_chjBdQpjlk
1785276556094427	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwzAI		item.create	bn-id4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe Phase A exit's triple-surface check (plan §21): Die Hard and Dining Philosophers checked through native API, CLI, and agent client with IDENTICAL artifacts — proving prose/CLI are projections of one truth, not parallel implementations.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Same snapshot+intent through all three surfaces yields byte-identical evidence artifacts and receipts (content-addressed equality, not just equal verdicts).\n- [ ] Pinned as a permanent regression (gate criteria stay regressions after closure, §21.1).\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","aci"],"parent":"bn-19p","size":"s","title":"Phase A exit verification: identical artifacts across API, CLI, and agent client"}	blake3:23pHFtyuBKaKnbNJtj0gLD7vaSMZ26iPprGVZXj0m6c
1785276556165856	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwzQI		item.create	bn-3dr	{"description":"# Context & Background\nG1 bullet (plan §4.5, §22): daemon crash recovery leaves no stale index entries or orphan tasks. Distinct from per-task cancellation (PR 6): this is whole-daemon kill-and-restart at adversarial points, including mid-publication (INV-017 interaction).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Crash-injection harness kills the daemon at instrumented points; restart reconciles to a state with no stale index entries, no orphan tasks, no half-published artifacts.\n- [ ] Recovery is itself deterministic and evidenced (recovery report artifact).\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","kernel"],"parent":"bn-19p","size":"m","title":"Daemon crash recovery: no stale index entries or orphan tasks [G1]"}	blake3:0bRr1a7ots8IL0XVHdPnrl3M15PCpshuaxhtLdCdqAw
