1785276556891848	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEw1wI		item.create	bn-136	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPhase B deliverable inside the §21 adapter bullet, operationally distinct from PR 14's journaling: the conformance corpus that pins the semantic-hook contract, run in CI against upstream asupersync versions N and N−1 AND upstream pre-releases, so an upstream breaking change is detected before release and opens a scheduled adapter epoch (§4.6) visible in envelopes.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Conformance corpus covers every journaled primitive class (lifecycle, reserve/commit/abort, cancellation phases, obligations, virtual time, channels).\n- [ ] CI matrix: N, N−1, and upstream pre-release; a pre-release break files an adapter-epoch event, not a silent red build.\n# Serves\nThe adapter is the product's foundation-contact with the real runtime; this corpus is what makes \"supported upstream window\" a checked claim instead of a hope.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","adapter"],"parent":"bn-3zt","size":"m","title":"Adapter conformance corpus and upstream N/N−1 CI lane"}	blake3:09TtQehdfP7MR3efPPdCDMMxrn97l8biG2LAE1HnZco
