1785276696454328	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEw_gI		item.create	bn-eu2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPhase C exit / G5 bullet with no owning PR: semantic artifacts are BYTE-IDENTICAL across the docs/19 determinism matrix — worker counts, build modes, platforms, hash seeds. This is the harness that proves it continuously, not once.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CI matrix varies workers/build-mode/platform/hash-seed and diffs artifact bytes; any divergence fails with the responsible stage named.\n# Serves\nDeterminism is the precondition for content-addressed reuse and for every \"identical artifacts\" claim in the plan.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-c","incremental"],"parent":"bn-1fd","size":"m","title":"docs/19 determinism matrix harness (byte-identical artifacts) [G5]"}	blake3:DD_0bjdfahl1UmUzmU6jDqTNEyv3hp7vP9zaoDm0FDM
1785276696526102	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEw_wI		item.create	bn-2ee	{"description":"# Context & Background\nPhase C exit / G5: the edit/check/explain loop must meet the docs/34 latency table (p50/p95 per interaction, including the explain-interaction row: failure → rendered causal explanation) on the reference workload — and G5 measures it WITH a saturating background swarm present (plan §4.1). This bone builds the measurement harness and reference workload; the swarm generator arrives with the Phase F workbench (measurement is re-run then).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Harness measures every docs/34 row (p50/p95) reproducibly on the reference workload; results published as evidence artifacts; regression-gated in CI.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-c","incremental","ux"],"parent":"bn-1fd","size":"m","title":"docs/34 latency instrumentation and gate-normative benchmark harness [G5]"}	blake3:CArOg5MIzlUtD3j1BwFyOX_mkG_Ev2n6qlICXARHzgE
1785276696601223	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwgAM		item.create	bn-qxx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nG5 bullet with no owning PR: evidence queries and context compilation meet the docs/34 targets at ≥10^7 evidence nodes on the reference workload. Requires a synthetic-but-realistic graph generator (shape from real Phase B/C usage distributions).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] 10^7-node graph generated deterministically; query and context-compilation latencies meet docs/34 targets; results recorded as G5 evidence.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-c","evidence","incremental"],"parent":"bn-1fd","size":"m","title":"Evidence-graph scale test: docs/34 targets at ≥10^7 nodes [G5]"}	blake3:5h8tqlLBFp3yYxGeWKWTw6eC9xYNje0S0hZMQtL2GB0
1785276696674825	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwgQM		item.create	bn-1p7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe §22 release-blocker doctrine binds every gate to the docs/09 soundness incident policy: a confirmed false-positive success verdict → block release, revoke affected claim IDs, publish affected semantic epochs, ship an artifact scanner, add a permanent regression, reevaluate the producing engine's certified-mode eligibility. The MACHINERY for that response (revocation propagation through the evidence graph, epoch publication, scanner scaffold) must exist before an incident does.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Claim revocation propagates through dependent evidence (dependents flip to invalidated, fail-closed).\n- [ ] Incident drill executed: a seeded false-positive is revoked end-to-end with scanner + regression artifacts produced.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-c","evidence","security"],"parent":"bn-1fd","size":"m","title":"Soundness-incident tooling: claim revocation, epoch publication, artifact scanner (docs/09)"}	blake3:PnGh2pDqUoyKzwsVjY9_-tXdZULXJP4Bkq06JecMu3A
1785276696746356	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwggM		item.create	bn-1kq3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSD-09 (PR 0) SPECIFIES the §4.5/§4.6/§4.7 operational contract; this bone IMPLEMENTS it: purge replacing content with Redacted(reason, commitment) stubs (schema mirrored across all §4.5-obligated artifact classes — SD-14, paid), backup and VERIFIED restore, the cross-user dedup existence-oracle rule, two-epoch migration with Preserved|Revalidate|Incompatible compatibility statements, engine-defect artifacts (§4.7). Sized l: one coherent daemon-storage workstream; split at implementation time if purge and migration land separately.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Purged content is unrecoverable but its commitment still verifies in receipts referencing it.\n- [ ] Restore is verified (content re-hashed against manifests), not trusted; dedup cannot act as a cross-user existence oracle.\n- [ ] A semantic-epoch advance migrates via the two-epoch window with per-artifact compatibility statements.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-c","kernel"],"parent":"bn-1fd","size":"l","title":"Operational contract implementation: purge/Redacted, backup + verified restore, two-epoch migration"}	blake3:J2fQmN_Rn0wGo_iFu0OGgSwA0rX1IMAzj1pUKjrXn88
1785276696818268	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwgwM		item.create	bn-2kzi	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe §16 bidirectional-editing hypothesis (G0-DX-08 validated the ambiguity-honesty artifact shape: multiple abstract candidates → typed conflict, never a silent choice). Lane work per research/31: build the DRIFT CORPUS (the lane deliverable — real abstract-edit/concrete-code pairs), measure the ambiguity rate, and implement lens v0 within whatever the rate supports. Kill: most real mappings too ambiguous, or users mistake candidate synchronization for verified preservation (measured under G8 instruments). Fallback: get-only projection + drift detection.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Drift corpus exists; ambiguity rate measured and recorded in research/31 (feeds the row's ratification).\n- [ ] Lens v0 (or the get-only fallback) ships with ambiguous edits yielding typed conflicts/obligations — never an invented choice (DX-08 pass condition at G6).\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-d","engine","research"],"parent":"bn-1db","size":"m","title":"Bidirectional lens v0 and drift corpus (research/31 lane) [G6]"}	blake3:TLanKmbei0gVvPNXI2DT0IVr7jEUG7DCXa0v75zFVYg
1785276696891818	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwhAM		item.create	bn-3aqb	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe benchmark CONTENT between the PR 10 harness and the Phase F public release: generate the §19 task suite from corpus families and the gaming corpus — diagnosis, repair, proof, synthesis task classes (continuumbench-task schema; 3 seed tasks exist in the dossier) — under §19.4 discipline: development/held-out family splits, source-hash isolation, deterministic grading. PR 30's end-to-end run and the G2 ablation draw from the development split; the held-out split waits for G9.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Development suite covers the §19 task classes with deterministic grading; held-out split generated and SEALED (access-logged, evaluated only at G9).\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-e","corpus","aci"],"parent":"bn-4rm","size":"m","title":"ContinuumBench task-suite construction (development/held-out splits, §19.4)"}	blake3:It_E0XLTMCZliN7yPw_HM1w7IFpI-dBIYs1WejKW68Q
1785276696964874	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwhQM		item.create	bn-1w93	{"description":"# Context & Background\nTwo quiet G10 bullets that need explicit ownership: DOCUMENTED assurance envelopes (what each lane/engine can and cannot claim, per migrated system and for the product generally) and operating-cost acceptability (measured cost of running Continuum on the migrated systems — compute, latency, maintenance).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Published envelope documentation covering every shipped lane (native, observed tokio, instrumented tokio, production monitoring).\n- [ ] Cost accounting from both migrations recorded against the G10 \"operating cost is acceptable\" bullet.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-f","docs","governance"],"parent":"bn-22h","size":"s","title":"Assurance-envelope documentation and operating-cost accounting [G10]"}	blake3:M5Vb9_viVhKiw2RJ-yO4I6NNhyii9p1VQIJ7Gj6InBg
