1785279105356090	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwxAM		item.create	bn-1grk	{"description":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase A (plan §21 exit, §22 G0/G1/G2, docs/52). Phases are gate-driven: this bone is closed by a HUMAN decision that the gates hold, not by child-completion.\n# Exit checklist (from plan §21 Phase A exit + gate bullets)\n- [ ] G0 freeze-blocking subset DX-01–03, 10, 12, 13, 14 all carry evidence in the matrix; §0.3 counts derived and green (validator).\n- [ ] Die Hard + Dining Philosophers identical artifacts across API/CLI/agent client.\n- [ ] ACI ablation won (or protocol redesigned before freeze) — DX-10.\n- [ ] Prompt-injection corpus cannot trigger privileged operations (G2).\n- [ ] Continuation resume validates epochs and inputs; daemon crash recovery clean (G1).\n- [ ] Gate criteria converted to permanent CI regressions (§21.1 hardening rule).\n- [ ] docs/52 + plan §22 G0/G1/G2 status updated in one reconciled commit.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","gate","exit-gate"],"parent":"bn-19p","size":"s","title":"Phase A exit gate: close G0 freeze subset, G1, G2"}	blake3:L2d0iRLOpT3WGToNZVF54Gi2WC4IgjN3f-xoNcXfb7E
1785279105447356	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwxQM		item.create	bn-1itt	{"description":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase B, anchored on the plan §25 \"brutally concrete\" end-to-end demonstration — the first full product loop on real code:\n1. Agent receives a 200-event failing run through a compact Context Pack; 2. identifies ack-before-durability; 3. proposes moving publication after sync; 4. Continuum proves intent unchanged; 5. exact replay passes; 6. neighboring cancellation/crash schedules pass; 7. property mutations and known mutants remain detectable; 8. refinement/certificate receipts rebuild; 9. a human reviews one compact semantic diff and receipt.\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] Nine-step demonstration runs end-to-end under the Phase B gate profile, producing a promotion receipt with NotYetEnforced gates listed honestly.\n- [ ] G3 development-suite bullets hold (all seven diff dimensions; Unknown blocks promotion).\n- [ ] G4 bullets hold including the real-failure (not only injected-mutant) diagnosis and repair.\n- [ ] Re-homed DX-04/DX-06 matrix rows carry evidence; docs/52 + plan §22 reconciled in one commit.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","gate","exit-gate"],"parent":"bn-3zt","size":"m","title":"Phase B exit gate: close G3, G4 — run the §25 nine-step demonstration"}	blake3:wSmgP2SLXy7r1Ivr0FRWojoCjXN_-qwtAOkKT9lCh-s
1785279105519340	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwxgM		item.create	bn-waj3	{"description":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase C (G5, plan §21 exit / §22 / docs/52).\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] docs/34 latency table met (p50/p95 incl. explain row) on the reference workload; swarm-present re-measurement scheduled for Phase F noted on the gate record.\n- [ ] Incremental Parity Audit trustworthy under differential audit; reuse-edge classes quarantining correctly; Conservative-collapse metric healthy (R21).\n- [ ] Reduction engines: zero reachability mismatch on the no-reduction corpus; certified claims fall back to unreduced (docs/08 R04).\n- [ ] Byte-identical artifacts across the docs/19 determinism matrix.\n- [ ] Evidence queries + context compilation meet docs/34 targets at ≥10^7 nodes.\n- [ ] docs/52 + plan §22 G5 reconciled in one commit.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-c","gate","exit-gate"],"parent":"bn-1fd","size":"s","title":"Phase C exit gate: close G5"}	blake3:Kl9wIzFsLtduAFbqXThTQImqTfbsKvZbyowJyCH3dcY
1785279105649402	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwxwM		item.create	bn-3cpt	{"description":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase D (G6, plan §21 exit / §22 / docs/52).\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] One nontrivial corpus protocol carries safety AND liveness evidence plus real-code refinement produced by the G6-holding proof service.\n- [ ] Kernel-checked Lean foundations, no placeholders; theorem+axiom manifests on every receipt; agent proof repair accepted only by kernel; certificate mutations rejected.\n- [ ] Proof Context Packs measurably improve proof-worker success/cost.\n- [ ] Re-homed DX-08/DX-11 matrix rows carry evidence; gate 9 enters the promotion profile; docs/52 + plan §22 reconciled.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-d","gate","exit-gate"],"parent":"bn-1db","size":"s","title":"Phase D exit gate: close G6"}	blake3:y8ds_QCAUWtnnBbFplPF1fxRtrQvV7cBVLzXADPSE6M
1785279105734396	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwyAM		item.create	bn-o1oy	{"description":"# Context\nManual gate-closure review for Phase E (G7, plan §21 exit / §22 / docs/52), plus the plan §25 from-scratch synthesis demonstration (ack_guard = synced through typed holes + finite CEGIS).\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] Rediscovery suite closed; at least one behaviorally novel candidate independently verified within its declared envelope.\n- [ ] Semantic (not syntactic) archive spread; hidden-variant generalization; unrealizability distinct from unknown with reusable evidence where supported.\n- [ ] Materialization produces model + Rust skeleton + proof obligations for a promoted candidate.\n- [ ] Re-homed DX-07 matrix row carries evidence; docs/48 preregistration published; docs/52 + plan §22 reconciled.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-e","gate","exit-gate"],"parent":"bn-4rm","size":"s","title":"Phase E exit gate: close G7"}	blake3:Zw8474T-ZGg9aDvuszWPo2o8e7QOSMiaq0u0uA9YvzA
1785279105818672	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwyQM		item.create	bn-39yh	{"description":"# Context\nThe 1.0 release review (plan §21 Phase F exit, §22 G8/G9/G10, docs/52, §23 success metrics). The release-blocker doctrine applies in full: any misleading assurance result, replay failure, stale receipt, hidden intent change, or unauthorized promotion blocks release regardless of feature completeness.\n# Exit checklist\n- [ ] G8: preregistered study results meet fixed thresholds (or the redesign path was taken and re-passed).\n- [ ] G9: 80 families at declared INTERACTION parity under held-out discipline; DX-15 closed; held-out gaming suite evaluated once.\n- [ ] G10: two-system criterion (identical in §21/§22/docs/52); agent repair in real review use; INV-008 production classifications valid; public ContinuumBench; documented envelopes; acceptable operating cost; zero known unprivileged false-promotion paths.\n- [ ] Corpus checkpoint 1.0 recorded; 1.x maintenance lane opened outside the phase ladder.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-f","gate","exit-gate"],"parent":"bn-22h","size":"m","title":"Phase F / 1.0 exit gate: close G8, G9, G10"}	blake3:yBUo7Y0GZMCexN-6tAyZgxbTo5RQRSnMllL8y5ZTmAc
1785279105899909	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwygM		item.create	bn-20jv	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCross-cutting quality floor for a project whose product claim IS correctness. Established in Phase A so every later crate inherits it: cargo-fuzz targets for every wire-input surface (native protocol frames, wire-form certificates — the kernel checks wire form, so wire form is the attack surface), property-test suites (proptest) for canonical encoding/total order, snapshot Merkle identities, and idempotency-key semantics; sanitizers (ASan/TSan on the daemon) and loom/deterministic-schedule tests for the CAS/publication and task-lifecycle concurrency. Complements, not replaces, PR 9's certificate mutation tests and the plan's own formal machinery.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fuzz targets run continuously in CI with corpus persistence; a seeded known-bad input proves each target actually bites.\n- [ ] Property suites cover encoding round-trip/total-order laws, snapshot identity, and idempotency invariants.\n- [ ] TSan/loom coverage over PR 2 publication and PR 6 lifecycle paths.\n# Serves\n\"Fail-closed\" is an architecture claim; fuzzing and property testing are how we keep the implementation honest about it between gate reviews.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","quality"],"parent":"bn-19p","size":"m","title":"Quality harness: property-test suites, sanitizers, and fuzz infrastructure in CI"}	blake3:e5Ju_U-9mY0CggeI6CoRDvtcw6DolXN4zk1u6Fz51Ts
1785279106020548	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwywM		item.create	bn-1nmq	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe CML front end is a classic fuzz target (untrusted text → semantic identity). Fuzz continuum-cml-syntax (crashes, hangs, non-determinism) and property-test the pipeline laws: parse→format→parse round-trip (with PR 15b), elaborate determinism (same source ⇒ same semantic identity), and out-of-fragment rejection totality.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fuzz targets for parser + elaborator in the CI fuzz lane, no crashes/hangs on the persisted corpus.\n- [ ] Property suites pin the three pipeline laws.\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-b","cml","quality"],"parent":"bn-3zt","size":"s","title":"CML parser/elaborator fuzzing and grammar property tests"}	blake3:TAWKdLSj8b9HhhWEuDMJe_I74yX5uR6hQ-lplxkVVLg
1785279106109032	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwzAM		item.create	bn-28ur	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe dossier (plan.md, docs/52, G0 matrix, §24.5 register, §25 ledger) is self-checking via tools/validate_dossier.py (25 checks: derived G0 counts, program status, spec-debt predicates, register quote identity, plan↔docs/52 bullet correspondence). Once implementation starts, the dossier must stay TRUE, not just internally consistent: matrix rows flip as DX items close, §0.3 counts re-derive, register rows ratify with quote-id markers, owner rows fill, RFCs stay normative as code lands.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the dossier validator in the implementation repo's CI (uv run --with jsonschema python tools/validate_dossier.py; regenerate validation-results.json + MANIFEST via tools/generate_manifest.py in the canonical order).\n- Adopt the one-commit reconciliation rule (§22): any gate-status or bullet change lands in plan §22 and docs/52 together.\n- Each phase exit-gate bone includes its dossier updates; this bone establishes the mechanism.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Validator green in CI on every merge; a PR that flips a DX row without updating §0.3 (or edits §25 without its predicate) fails CI.\n","kind":"task","labels":["docs","governance"],"parent":"bn-3dl","size":"s","title":"Dossier↔implementation sync discipline: validator in CI, living-document updates per gate"}	blake3:Nh3YDdPlytsZdYx9BGmDv7FgCxzvth4GNODZTj3wzSc
1785279106189799	claude	itc:v3:AWL5JJk5zz5JJEAAAAAAQfqrXd76qgAAAAEwzQM		item.create	bn-281l	{"description":"# Context & Background\nG8 demands workflows learnable without formal-methods folklore; G10 demands documented assurance envelopes and real migrations. That requires real user documentation, distinct from the dossier: CLI reference (golden-test-derived from PR 13's pinned output), the edit/check/explain and debug/repair tutorials (the docs/34 workflows), the tokio onboarding path (observed → instrumented lane), and the migration guide distilled from Migrations A/B.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CLI reference generated/checked against PR 13 golden outputs (cannot drift).\n- [ ] Tutorials for the three human docs/34 workflows; formative-session feedback incorporated.\n- [ ] Migration guide validated by the second migration (Migration B follows the written guide, gaps filed as doc bugs).\n","kind":"task","labels":["phase-f","docs","ux"],"parent":"bn-22h","size":"m","title":"User-facing documentation: CLI reference, tutorials, migration guide"}	blake3:rXGFA2VDQ9R2RvVs4eUzmevFjUuRXpIQGepZmdsKWwI
